cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below. The bills come from the US Energy Information Administration (EIA-861M); the home and end-use shapes from EIA's 2020 Residential Energy Consumption Survey."
type: dataset
title: "Average Electric Bill by State, Home Type and End Use (US, monthly since 2010)"
abstract: >
  What US homes pay for electricity each month, for every state and the US, every month since January 2010,
  from the utilities' own returns to the US Energy Information Administration (EIA-861M: residential revenue
  divided by residential customers). Each bill is split by type of home, bedrooms, floor area, people, heating
  fuel and tenure, and by end use, using ratios and shares from EIA's 2020 Residential Energy Consumption Survey
  microdata (18,496 homes) with jackknife standard errors; the change since 2010 is split exactly into a price
  part and a use part. Includes a check of the survey against the utility returns for 2020.
